<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Align="Align.Justify">
	These projects I've been part of since Feb 24, when I started working for
	<MudLink Href="https://www.landing.brainassistant.de/en" Target="_blank">brainboost</MudLink>
	full-time. So far I've had a lot of fun there, learned a LOT and am looking forward to working on even more projects in the future.<br/>
	At brainboost we are constantly working on improving our Neurofeedback software: the BrainAssistant. 
	However, Neurofeedback works best if you have good games & apps to use for training, which is where I came in originally.
	My first almost entirely new project was the NeuroRacer (see below) and it was a great success with both our direct Neurofeedback clients as well as our business customers.
	But alas I found myself drifting more and more into classical software development, such as helping out with development of the BrainAssitant, webtools, and data exports for research partners.
	Right now my main areas of work are split about evenly between game and software development, but I also do technical customer support.<br/>
	Below you can find a short summary of the projects I want to highlight the most.
</MudText>

